# apply_tsg_intrabar_skip_partial.py — ── TSG_MTM_INTRABAR_20261031 ── ── RECORDED_SKIP_PARTIAL_20261031 ──
#
# From the 14–30 Oct Tigris backtest vs paper review (31 Oct):
# 1. SKIP PARTLY RECORDED DAYS. Recorded-data runs drop the option rows of
#    every day the recorder graded anything but 'clean' (mid-October days held
#    5–54 % of the chain: 16 Oct picked four different strikes, 26 Oct put
#    shorts and wings on the same strike). Spot stays for indicator warm-up.
#    The run's summary carries recorded_skipped_days; the Run tab's banner
#    lists the skipped days of the chosen range.
# 2. TIGRIS MTM TARGET / SL CHECKED INTRABAR (runner logic, as the live
#    engine). Live checks the basket MTM on every tick; the runner only saw
#    each minute's close (29 Oct: live MTM_SL 14:26, backtest 14:56). Now each
#    open leg is also valued at the minute's adverse extreme (SELL → high,
#    BUY → low; synthetic legs → their mark). When that worst case crosses
#    −SL and the close does not, the basket exits AT THAT MINUTE at prices
#    interpolated between close and extreme so the combined MTM lands on
#    −SL — where live's market exit fires. The target gets the mirror check on
#    the favourable extreme. Trail and IV stops stay on the close.
#    Config mtm_check: "intrabar" (DEFAULT — new runs, parity) | "close"
#    (every run before today). Backtest → TSG form: "MTM check" selector.
#    !! Tigris results change: more / earlier MTM exits than the sealed
#    numbers, which used the minute close. Re-run the seal with INTRABAR.
#
#   EDIT backend/app/backtest/tsg/backtest_tsg_runner.py · test_tsg_runner.py (+5)
#        backend/app/backtest/queue_worker.py · api/backtest_routes.py
#        frontend/src/pages/Backtest.jsx · backend/app/recorder/test_seam.py (19)
#   Requires apply_recorded_source_fix2.py.
#
#   cd <repo root> && python3 apply_tsg_intrabar_skip_partial.py [repo_root] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]
